A||N||3||Warhawk||Fiero Fuel economy||||1||
Z||000000||Warhawk||12-22-1999||08:12 PM||||Howdy, I'm a brand new Fiero owner, so new I haven't even driven it yet! My Fiero is an '86 2M4, great condition except that the motor is locked up.  I'm having a rebuilt longblock installed to rectify that. What kind of fuel economy can I expect from this one?  It's the 2.5 4 banger. I currently drive an '86 Toyota 4x4 pickup (2.4L) and am '88 Suzuki Samurai (1.3L) so I'm not accustomed to much power. I'm planning to use the Fiero for a work car, I drive about 20K a year for my job.<P>Thanks, and Merry Christmas!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||12-22-1999||08:16 PM||||My 85 SE with the 4 cyl and 5 speed gets around 25-32 mpg. Not too bad for a 15 year old car!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||12-22-1999||09:57 PM||||Welcome to Fierodom!  Our 84SE 2M4 (2.5)auto,with a 10,000 mi. old rebuild, averages 30mpg.  That's mostly in town trips.  Gets better on interstate.  Again, not bad for a 2 seater gocart, with heat, air,tilt, cruise,pw, pdl,pm, stereo, that you can drive in the rain.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Sage (edited 12-22-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||10:46 PM||||This has been in at least one or two other threads.  Use the search function and look them up.  There's more info than you could ever use. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  And congratulations on becoming a Fiero owner.  This and loosing your virginity will be 2 of the biggest moments in your life.  (At least I got one accomplished)<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 12-22-1999).]||||reg||1
